Package: CrossDomainAdjust
Type: Package
Title: Trainable Feature Encoding and Partial Cross-Domain Adjustment
Version: 2.1.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Weikaixin", family = "Kong", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "weikaixin.kong@aalto.fi")
Description: Fits reusable raw, within-sample rank, or binary gene-pair
    representations, optional training-fitted feature standardization,
    and partial cross-domain feature transformations. Binary
    pairs are screened using training-set prevalence, with blockwise candidate
    evaluation and optional feature caps. Domain centering and low-rank
    projection support continuous adjustment strengths and frozen application
    to new samples. Includes fold-local tuning and descriptive diagnostics.
    Domain-associated variation is not assumed to be purely technical.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: stats, utils
Suggests: survival
URL: https://github.com/weikaixi/CrossDomainAdjust
BugReports: https://github.com/weikaixi/CrossDomainAdjust/issues
NeedsCompilation: no
